  "details": "There seems to be a bug where some object sync information is preserved across instances, resulting in pickups being in the wrong location among other things.\n\nFor this to occur, the object must be disabled when you join the instance, as well as when you leave. Additionally, it requires at least two people.\n\nI have made a test world that demonstrates the bug.\n\n1. Go to https://vrchat.com/home/world/wrld_102b885e-4104-41c8-8dfc-87968eb97d51 with two people\n\n2. Click on the red cube to enable and teleport the yellow key relatively close to you\n\n3. Pick up the key and take it to the grey platform\n\n4. Click the pink cube to disable the key object\n\n5. The instance master should rejoin the world\n\n6. Both users should create a new instance (and perhaps the original instance master needs to go in first?)\n\n7. In the new instance, click the blue cube to enable the door and the key\n\n8. The key should be where it was left in the previous instance and thus usable with the door (by default it's very far away at coordinates 1M, 1M, 1M)\n\nIt seems that the ownership transfer that happens when the instance master rejoins gets queued up but doesn't fire because the objects are disabled, and instead gets fired the next time the objects are enabled, even if it's in another instance.\n\nWhile this is a rather contrived example, I've also seen this bug more subtly in proper worlds like Crystal Defenders. I also wouldn't be surprised if these sync events not being flushed are tangentially related to that issue where the user that first spawns into a world gets flung very far away, but who knows.",
